# Netlify redirect / access rules
#
# The repository root IS the publish directory (netlify.toml: publish = "."),
# which puts .git/ inside the deployed tree. Netlify normally strips it, but
# this is a belt-and-braces guard so repository internals can never be fetched
# over HTTP whatever the host does with dotfiles.
#
# Anything under /.git/ returns 404 rather than being served.
/.git/*  /  404
